From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 06:15:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] presentation: panorama auto columns fit book covers and wide
 covers span two lanes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A folded phone showed only two panorama columns, so tall covers looked
oversized. 168 dp was chosen so a single-column 3:2 cover would not be
cramped. One minimum cannot suit both shapes.

Auto columns are book-sized again: 104 dp, from
lanes = (available + 4) / (min + 4) with available = window width minus
the 16 dp horizontal padding. That is 3 columns at 360, 420, and 459 dp.
A wide cover uses PanoramaSpan.TwoLanesWhenRoomy: two adjacent lanes when
there are at least three, otherwise one. Related-work panorama grids,
which Anikku has and Mihon does not, use the same span.

与 mihon-harmony 0023 同源. The column constant stays in PanoramaGrid.kt,
which is where Anikku already resolves auto columns for the shelf, browse,
and related grids.
