+/**
+ * How a [PanoramaSpan.TwoLanesWhenRoomy] cell picks its column pair, always inside the recess limit.
+ * [Leftmost] is the reading-order rule. [LeastWaste] prefers the eligible pair whose shorter
+ * lane loses the least area (a tie stays on the left).
+ */
+enum class PanoramaPairPick {
+    Leftmost,
+    LeastWaste,
+}
+
+/**
+ * Production pair rule.
+ *
+ * A fixed-seed study (200 cells, 3 and 6 columns, 10/30/50% wide) keeps the reading-order rule.
+ * Its holes stay under 2.4% of cell area plus holes, below the 8% line where a least-waste pick
+ * would be worth the extra upward jumps. Least-waste is still implemented so the study can rerun.
+ */
+val PANORAMA_PAIR_PICK = PanoramaPairPick.Leftmost
